# ops/runtime/ - mutable runtime state, written atomically.
#
# Holds health.json, supervisor_health.json and any pid file. Every file in
# here is written by the tmp-then-replace path in ops/health.py, so a reader
# polling mid-write never sees a partial document.
#
# This marker is tracked so the directory exists in a fresh clone. .gitignore
# ignores the CONTENTS (`ops/runtime/*`) and re-admits this one file with a
# negation. A bare `ops/runtime/` rule would swallow the marker too, and git
# will not re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded - which is why
# the rule is written against the contents rather than the directory.
